#### 4. Numeric claims without footnotes (blocker partially resolved through condensation and renumbering)

The pre-gate draft reported 50 numeric claims without footnotes. This count combined three
distinct populations:

**Population A — Numbers in the Decisions section without footnoted backing.** These included:
analyst-constructed dollar ranges ($250K–$500K per module template change), square-footage
estimates (25,000–40,000 sq ft for lounge-capable shells), and percentage estimates
("single-digit percent" of modular savings eroded by bespoke features). These did not appear in
the evidence ledger at any evidence ID.

*Resolution:* Removed by condensing the Decisions section (see Word Count change above). No
attempt to footnote analyst estimates not grounded in evidence records.

**Population B — The 50% missed-connections claim (CL-36 in pre-gate lineage).** This claim
appeared in the body with no footnote marker and no evidence IDs in the pre-gate lineage.

*Resolution:* Added footnote [^26] after verifying the primary source. Direct WebFetch of
View from the Wing ("American Airlines Rebuilt Its Dallas Hub — Missed Connections Are Down
50%," 2026) confirmed the figure as DFW hub head Jim Moses's statement at an internal AA
employee meeting covering April 7–23, 2026. The AA newsroom's own "Forever Forward" release was
also confirmed as describing strong qualitative results for the same period. Footnote [^26] cites
both, with explicit qualification that the 50% figure is AA's own internal data from a short
initial window, not independently audited. Body text reflects this qualification: "American's own
initial data for its first seventeen days showed a 50% reduction in missed connections — the
airline's own figure, from an employee briefing in a short initial window."

**Population C — Numbers in the body that were already footnoted, but whose footnote markers
were misnumbered due to the sequence error.** These appeared to have no footnotes only because
the sequence error prevented the gate from correctly matching markers to definitions.

*Resolution:* Fixed by the complete footnote renumbering in Change 2 above.

**Result:** All numeric claims in the final draft carry footnotes. Analyst-estimated ranges
without evidence backing were removed.

